    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0481" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg379"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89/954</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Economic Adviser</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Feis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-05-31">May 31, 1935</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The President has given his approval to the form of the June 15 debt notes and to
                    the further suggestion that the idea of payments in kind and special materials
                    might be broached to the British and Belgian Ambassadors. All the debt notices
                    have been sent to CR<anchor n="9" xml:id="d265-f1"/> for <pb facs="0482" n="380"
                        xml:id="pg380"/> despatch in the regular way. You may wish to ask the
                    Ambassadors to come in to talk with you early next week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H[<hi rendition="#small-caps">erbert</hi>] F[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >eis</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
